# CPE UoE Part 3 Word formation — unified grey shell

When adding or editing **Part 3 gap-fill** pages under `use-of-english/part3-word-formation/`:

## Shared stylesheet

- **`css/cpe-uoe-part3-wf-shell.css`** — link from every new standard Part 3 page:
  ```html
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="../../css/cpe-uoe-part3-wf-shell.css" />
  ```
- Put `<body class="cpe-p3-body">` on the page shell.

## One grey family (mandatory)

Do **not** mix cyan-tinted example boxes, ad-hoc hex borders, and `--line` on the same screen.

| Token | Use |
|-------|-----|
| **`--cpe-p3-line`** (`#324a71`) | **All** borders: page, header rule, `.example` / `.block`, gap inputs, hub footer |
| **`--cpe-p3-panel-soft`** | Background for **both** example box and main text block |
| **`--cpe-p3-muted`** | Instruction body, block title, example label |
| **`--cpe-p3-muted-dim`** | Tags, score line, secondary meta |
| **`--cpe-p3-gap-bg`** | Gap input fill (not a second blue) |

## Forbidden on standard Part 3 pages

- `rgba(56, 189, 248, …)` borders/backgrounds on `.example` / `.example-box`
- Hardcoded `#4d6fa1`, `#d5e2f8`, `#7dd3fc`, `#bae6fd` for borders or body grey text
- Inline `<style>` blocks duplicating the full shell — extend the shared CSS or add a **tiny** page-only override (e.g. `.page--wide`)

## Accent colours (allowed)

- Links / back: `--cpe-p3-accent`
- Caps roots: `--cpe-p3-caps`
- Check button gradient, ok/bad gap states — unchanged

## Exceptions

- **Flip-card hub** (`part3-word-formation/index.html`) and **hearts trainer** (`unit5-listening-en-en-hearts.html`) may keep local layout CSS; still use **`--cpe-p3-line`** / **`--cpe-p3-panel-soft`** for any panel borders added there.

## Checklist

- [ ] Example box visually matches main block (same border + background)?
- [ ] Gap inputs use `--cpe-p3-line`, not a lighter blue?
- [ ] Instruction text uses `--cpe-p3-muted`, not `#d5e2f8`?
